# healthie's block for the shared reverse proxy on the box.
#
# NOTHING IN THIS REPO APPLIES THIS FILE. /etc/caddy/Caddyfile is owned outright
# by the home-proxy repo, whose deploy installs its own copy wholesale and
# publishes an mDNS alias for every `http://<name>.local` it declares. Two
# repositories writing that file would mean each one silently reverting the
# other, so healthie's deploy does not touch Caddy at all — it only warns when
# healthie.local does not reach it.
#
# To route healthie: paste this block into home-proxy/deploy/Caddyfile, commit
# it there, and run that repo's deploy. The mDNS alias comes along with it.
#
# The `http://` prefix is load-bearing: it pins the site to port 80 and disables
# automatic HTTPS, which no public CA will issue for a `.local` name.
#
# 3005 is healthie-backend's default listen port and is registered to healthie
# on this box (3000 fewd, 3001 chorez, 3002 kammerz).
#
# Validated against the box's own caddy 2.6.2, both standalone and composed into
# home-proxy's Caddyfile.

http://healthie.local {
	reverse_proxy localhost:3005
}
